<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/ashanti-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ashanti%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ashanti Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Yaa Asantewaa leads the War of the Golden Stool against British rule</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kanem-bornu-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kanem-Bornu%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kanem-Bornu Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">French forces kill Rabih at Kousseri; Britain, France and Germany partition the territory</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/sokoto-caliphate"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Sokoto%20Caliphate.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Sokoto Caliphate</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Frederick Lugard proclaims the Protectorate of Northern Nigeria</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-buganda"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Buganda.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Buganda</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Buganda Agreement makes the kingdom a privileged part of the Uganda Protectorate</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/orange-free-state"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Orange%20Free%20State.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Orange Free State</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Bloemfontein falls to Lord Roberts and Britain annexes the state as the Orange River Colony</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-tonga"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Tonga.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Tonga</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A Treaty of Friendship makes Tonga a British protected state</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/minoan-civilisation"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Minoan%20civilisation.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Minoan civilisation</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Arthur Evans begins to excavate the palace of Knossos</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/pan-africanism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Pan-Africanism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Pan-Africanism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Henry Sylvester Williams’s Pan-African Conference meets in London; W. E. B. Du Bois drafts its address</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-dagbon"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Dagbon.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Dagbon</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 7 April Friedrich Rigler's German expedition attacks the Dagomba who had fled to Sang in British territory, kills at least 83, among them Andani's son Idi, and installs Alasan as Yaa Naa.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/winston-churchill"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Winston%20Churchill.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Winston Churchill</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">He is elected Conservative MP for Oldham, aged 25, after his escape from a Boer prisoner-of-war camp</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/pali-canon"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Pali%20Canon.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Pali Canon</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The first complete printed edition of the Canon appears in Burma, in 38 volumes</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/beijing"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Beijing.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Beijing</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Eight-Nation Alliance lifts the siege of the Legation Quarter and occupies the city</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/kumasi"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kumasi.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kumasi</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Ashanti besiege Governor Hodgson in the fort until he breaks out on 23 June</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/mogao-caves"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mogao%20Caves.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mogao Caves</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Wang Yuanlu found the walled-up cave full of manuscripts</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/yaa-asantewaa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Yaa%20Asantewaa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Yaa Asantewaa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Asante lay siege to the British fort at Kumasi; she is chosen war leader of the Asante forces</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/empress-dowager-cixi"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Empress%20Dowager%20Cixi.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Empress Dowager Cixi</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">She supports the Boxers and declares war on the foreign powers; the court flees Beijing for Xi'an</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/ahmadiyya"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ahmadiyya.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ahmadiyya</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">In a manifesto dated 4 November, Ahmad announces that the movement will be named for Muhammad's alternative name Ahmad</span></li></ul></section>
